  "rawText": "At age 23, he married Doris Louise Farrow and moved\n\nEQ Washi nggon,;. D.C..\n\nHe held various positions in the private sector of D.C.,\nbefore accepting an appointment with the United States\nDepartment of the Navy. He was assigned to work at the\n\nNaval Gun Factory, as a Cartridge Case Maker.\n\nWhen World War II ended, he left the Gun Factory and\nbegan working for the Federal Housing Administration as\n\nae Clerk she remained there until his retirement an 7972.\n\nAfter retiring, he had more time to devote to his\nHobby. His dream was to design an efficient Rotary Engine\nuSing centrifugal force. He drew hundreds of plans and\nmade several prototypes but, none had the precision\nnecessary to perform the way that he had envisioned. He\nnever gave up trying to improve his designs. (See next\npage.) ——\n\nHis motto was: \" Stay on an even keel and always\n\nmake decisions based on principles rather than emotions.”\n\nHe passed away, March 15, 1986. He left behind, his\nwife, Louise and four offspring: ; a\nEleanor Patricia\nMildred Elaine\nJoan Alease\n\nLynwood Wayne",
  "cleanedText": "At age 23, he married Doris Louise Farrow and moved\n\nEQ Washi nggon,;. D.C..\n\nHe held various positions in the private sector of D.C.,\nbefore accepting an appointment with the United States\nDepartment of the Navy. He was assigned to work at the\n\nNaval Gun Factory, as a Cartridge Case Maker.\n\nWhen World War II ended, he left the Gun Factory and\nbegan working for the Federal Housing Administration as\n\nae Clerk she remained there until his retirement an 7972.\n\nAfter retiring, he had more time to devote to his\nHobby. His dream was to design an efficient Rotary Engine\nuSing centrifugal force. He drew hundreds of plans and\nmade several prototypes but, none had the precision\nnecessary to perform the way that he had envisioned. He\nnever gave up trying to improve his designs. (See next\npage.) ——\n\nHis motto was: \" Stay on an even keel and always\n\nmake decisions based on principles rather than emotions.”\n\nHe passed away, March 15, 1986. He left behind, his\nwife, Louise and four offspring: ; a\nEleanor Patricia\nMildred Elaine\nJoan Alease\n\nLynwood Wayne",
